<div style="font-weight: bold; text-align: center;">
<p><em><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PEI2zet48Uc">For your consideration.</a></em></p>
</div>
<hr />
<p><em>She's the dedicated researcher with nothing to lose. He's an anomalous typewriter with dreams too big to last. And in the middle of it all is Murphy Law — the man you call when everything that can go wrong… does.</em></p>
<p><em>Watch them explode across the silver-screen in tonight's premier: <strong>Murphy Law in… TYPE 3043 — FOR MURDER!</strong></em></p>
<hr />
<p><strong>SOURCES:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Image is from <a href="https://pixabay.com/en/typewriter-antique-old-1782011/">here</a>.</li>
<li>Inspired by a Marauder of mine from a <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mage:_The_Ascension">Mage: The Ascension</a> campaign, my childhood love for <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Raymond_Chandler">Raymond Chandler</a> and <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dashiell_Hammett">Dashiell Hammett</a> novels, and &#8212; most of all &#8212; <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Calvin_and_Hobbes">Calvin and Hobbes</a> for providing the prototype of Murphy Law: Tracer Bullet.</li>
<li>Additional credit should go to <a href="/dr-adileh-khayyam-s-personnel-file">Taffeta</a>'s <a href="/to-be-noir-not-to-be">To Be Noir Not To Be</a>, which was another inspiration for Murphy Law's whole schtick.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>FEEDBACK:</strong></p>
<ul>
