			<div class="content" id="post-content-2962494">
									

<p>I'm not seeing a hidden collapsible on that page (but I guess that's the point?).</p>
<p>I <strong>am</strong> super-tempted to have a hidden collapsible with a closing credits scene where&#8230;</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>O5-5 and Murphy meet on the docks with O5-5's bodyguards; Murphy tells him it's done &#8212; O5-5 asks how they'll get in contact with him if they ever need him again, Murphy just says &quot;I'll be around&quot;, and starts to walk off into the distance&#8230;</p>
<p>&#8230;then one of O5-5's bodyguards step forward, drawing his firearm, saying &quot;We can't just let him go, he's an <em>anomaly</em>, we have to contain him&#8212;&quot;</p>
<p>And the O5-5 stops him with one hand &#8212; lights his cigarette &#8212; and says &#8212; &quot;Forget it, Jake. It's Chinatown.&quot;</p>
<p>Camera fades on Murphy's silhouette walking away. Credits roll. O5-5 name is censored.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p><strong>ETA:</strong> Oh, you meant SCP-2316! I remember how that one works.</p>
<p><strong>ETA 2:</strong> Here's what I came up with. Little worried it would push this deep into 'SCP-J' territory, but it fits Murphy's style:</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">(would&nbsp;be&nbsp;hidden)</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">...</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p><tt>FADE IN:</tt></p>
<p><tt>EXT. DOCKS - SUNSET</tt></p>
<p><tt>MURPHY stands at the edge of the docks, watching the sun go down on just another day. Behind him, two sleek black cars roll up. A dozen men start pouring out of them, but he doesn't bother to look back.</tt></p>
<p><tt>The men are smartly dressed in black suits; they crowd around a short old woman dressed in white. She slowly approaches MURPHY, leaning heavily on her cane. One man follows her closely &#8212; her personal secretary and bodyguard.</tt></p>
<p><tt>The man is AGENT JULY; whatever it is, he does it by the books. The woman is O5-5 &#8212; and if we told you anything else, we'd have to kill you.</tt></p>
<p><tt>O5-5 moves to watch the sunset besides MURPHY. AGENT JULY is clearly displeased; he'd rather her not get too close.</tt></p>
<p style="text-align: center;"><tt><strong>O5-5</strong></tt></p>
<blockquote>
<p><tt>You did some good work today, Mr. Law.</tt></p>
</blockquote>
<p style="text-align: center;"><tt><strong>MURPHY</strong></tt></p>
<blockquote>
<p><tt>Yeah.</tt></p>
</blockquote>
<p><tt>O5-5 reaches to pull a cigarette out of her pocket, placing it between her lips.</tt></p>
<p style="text-align: center;"><tt><strong>O5-5</strong></tt></p>
<blockquote>
<p><tt>If we ever need your services&#8230; how might we contact you?</tt></p>
</blockquote>
<p><tt>MURPHY leans forward and plucks the cigarette out of O5-5's mouth. AGENT JULY immediately reaches for his firearm, but O5-5 lifts her hand to stop him.</tt></p>
<p style="text-align: center;"><tt><strong>MURPHY</strong></tt></p>
<blockquote>
<p><tt>I'll be around.</tt></p>
</blockquote>
<p><tt>MURPHY turns, sliding the cigarette into his mouth and pulling out his lighter. As he walks away, he starts to light it &#8212; and a fog begins to roll in.</tt></p>
<p><tt>AGENT JULY steps forward, as if to go after MURPHY. O5-5 grabs him by the shoulder.</tt></p>
<p style="text-align: center;"><tt><strong>AGENT JULY</strong></tt></p>
<blockquote>
<p><tt>But &#8212; he's an anomaly. We can't let him go. We have to contain him&#8212;</tt></p>
</blockquote>
<p style="text-align: center;"><tt><strong>O5-5</strong></tt></p>
<blockquote>
<p><tt>(shaking her head)</tt></p>
<p><tt>Forget about it, July. It's Chinatown.</tt></p>
</blockquote>
<p><tt>AGENT JULY slides his hand away from his firearm. Together, they watch MURPHY walk off into the foggy night.</tt></p>
<p><tt>The camera focuses on MURPHY's silhouette as the view fades to black.</tt></p>
<p><tt>FADE OUT.</tt></p>
<p><tt>CREDITS ROLL:</tt><br /></p>
<div style="text-align: center;">
<blockquote>
<p><tt>DR. LEWIS played by&#8230;</tt><br />
<tt>MICHELLE LEWIS</tt></p>
<p><tt>SITE DIRECTOR AUGUST played by&#8230;</tt><br />
<tt>JEREMIAH AUGUST</tt></p>
<p><tt>SCP-3043 played by&#8230;</tt><br />
<tt>A 1937 OLYMPIA ELITE TYPE-WRITER</tt></p>
<p><tt>MURPHY LAW played by&#8230;</tt><br />
<tt>HIMSELF</tt></p>
<p><tt>AGENT JULY played by&#8230;</tt><br />
<tt>JULIAN JULY</tt></p>
<p><tt>O5-5 played by&#8230;</tt><br />
<tt>[REDACTED]</tt><br />
<br />
<br />
<tt>WITH SPECIAL THANKS TO SITE-95</tt></p>
<p><br />
<br />
<tt>LOOK FOR MURPHY LAW TO RETURN IN&#8230;</tt></p>
<p><tt>&#8230;THE FOUNDATION ALWAYS RINGS TWICE!</tt><br />
<br />
<br />
<br /></p>
<p style="text-align: center;"><tt><strong>THE END</strong></tt></p>
</blockquote>
</div>
