<p>This just kind of exacerbates my issue - it's an OP OC b.s.ing its way through the plot-points, and while I recognize that it's part of the character, I can't help but be disappointed that there's not a whole lot of substance to the story beyond a skip's noir wish-fulfillment. The actual format screw is well-done, the prose is right on-point and deliciously hammy, but I'm not sold on the narrative.</p>
