			<div class="content" id="post-content-2957285">
									

<p>I'm inclined to agree. Why did Murphy win? Because he's immune to the anomaly. Why doesn't 3043 make somebody stop him? Because he made them immune too. How does he have these capabilities? He just does.</p>
<p>There isn't a conflict here. Murphy struggles with nothing, and requires no visible effort to complete his mission.</p>
<p>But you have the style down pat, so I have hope for this yet. Perhaps he himself is immune to its effects, and can institute his Noir Override, but the typewriter can overwrite everything else. So he's left with a 'client' who insists that nothing is going on, falsified documentation that shows nothing suspicious, and site personnel who are only tolerating him because of a general sense that he &quot;fits in&quot; with this noir stuff&#8230; But he's still been called there, so clearly there must be work for him to do. So, you know, he has to properly hard-boil his way through a real mystery. That would be fun to read!</p>

							</div>

