<p>I'll think about this; part of the reason I decided not to make it a mystery is because of the limited format (and I was deeply worried that both Murphy and the writing style would start to grate on the reader if it went on too long, so I wanted to end things quickly before that happened).</p>
<p>If I did expand this into a genuine mystery, though, I'd probably need some help figuring a few things out.</p>
